<!-- One-page summary: three numbers side by side. The stat layout has a single value slot, so this is
     built in flow mode.

     Each card puts one picture under its number — the number gives the size, the picture the shape:
       - 47 min: a 47-cell strip that is red all the way (the whole span the incident covered).
       - 8.4%: the error-rate curve rises off the normal floor and comes back down (`type="path"`, a curve in a 0–100 box).
       - 12 min: a strip where only 12 of the 47 minutes (26%) are amber — a quarter of the incident went unnoticed.
     The two strip pieces are the two cells of `grid cols="12fr 35fr"`, so the ratio is the source numbers verbatim.

     The three numbers follow the deck's color rule (001_cover): 47 min and 8.4% are what the incident
     cost, so `accent5`; 12 min is where we were late, so `accent4`. Card height is never written as a
     number — the number grid takes everything between the title and the strip below with `grow="1"`. -->
<slide id="summary" enter="rise">
  <text variant="kicker">Summary</text>
  <h2>For 47 minutes, one in ten payments failed</h2>
  <grid cols="3" gap="md" grow="1">
    <shape variant="stat-card" type="rounded-rect" fill="surface" w="fill" pad="lg">
      <col gap="sm" h="fill" justify="center">
        <text role="title" size="88" color="accent5">47<span size="40"> min</span></text>
        <text role="body">of Payments API 5xx</text>
        <shape type="rect" fill="accent5" border="none" w="fill" h="10"/>
        <text role="caption">14:02 – 14:49 KST</text>
      </col>
    </shape>
    <shape variant="stat-card" type="rounded-rect" fill="surface" w="fill" pad="lg">
      <col gap="sm" h="fill" justify="center">
        <text role="title" size="88" color="accent5">8.4<span size="40">%</span></text>
        <text role="body">peak error rate</text>
        <stack w="fill" h="56">
          <shape type="path" fill="alpha(accent5, 0.25)" border="none" w="fill" h="fill" d="M0,96 H22 C30,96 32,4 40,4 C48,4 50,60 62,74 C72,86 80,94 100,96 V100 H0 Z"/>
          <shape type="path" fill="none" border="2 solid accent5" w="fill" h="fill" d="M0,96 H22 C30,96 32,4 40,4 C48,4 50,60 62,74 C72,86 80,94 100,96"/>
        </stack>
        <text role="caption">0.02% on a normal day</text>
      </col>
    </shape>
    <shape variant="stat-card" type="rounded-rect" fill="surface" w="fill" pad="lg">
      <col gap="sm" h="fill" justify="center">
        <text role="title" size="88" color="accent4">12<span size="40"> min</span></text>
        <text role="body">to detect</text>
        <grid cols="12fr 35fr" gap="0" w="fill">
          <shape type="rect" fill="accent4" border="none" w="fill" h="10"/>
          <shape type="rect" fill="alpha(muted, 0.35)" border="none" w="fill" h="10"/>
        </grid>
        <text role="caption">26% of the outage went unseen</text>
      </col>
    </shape>
  </grid>
  <grid cols="2" gap="lg">
    <col gap="xs">
      <text role="heading" size="24">What happened</text>
      <p size="20">120k payment cache keys expired in one second and hit the DB.
      The read pool ran dry; the API returned 5xx.</p>
    </col>
    <col gap="xs">
      <text role="heading" size="24" color="accent3">How it stopped</text>
      <p size="20"><strong>Load shedding</strong>, not a rollback. Once the cache
      refilled, errors were normal by 14:49.</p>
    </col>
  </grid>
  <note>Read the three numbers and move on. The detail comes later.</note>
</slide>
